From afe2c653d01e70ad1ea84c7a56133f6069e9e935 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hotty Agent <hotty@neuroplast.io>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 22:10:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Implement `text-overflow: ellipsis`

Stylo computes `text-overflow`, but nothing drew it, so a line of a box
that clips its overflow was cut mid-glyph at the edge and showed no
ellipsis.

Inline layout now shapes the end side's ellipsis (or string) in the
root's style. When an inline root with `overflow-x` other than `visible`
paints, each left-to-right line that runs past the content box's end
edge loses the clusters and atomic inlines that would sit under the
ellipsis: the text and children are drawn under a clip that ends the
line's band at its last whole cluster or inline box, and the ellipsis
is drawn right after it on the line's baseline. Each band runs from the
previous line's bottom to its own, so tall glyphs are not cut.

Rounding the layout to whole pixels can leave a box that was sized to
its line up to a pixel short of it. A line overflows only when it runs
past the unrounded edge as well, so rounding alone draws no ellipsis.

Right-to-left lines still clip without an ellipsis.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
